GCC.changelog = [["1.3.1", "2026-11-12", "Farmworker coverage recoded to follow the codebook rule (no exclusion of farm workers employed by firms = covered): Bahrain and Oman now covered, with household farm work under domestic-worker law; Saudi Arabia coded as a new category, separate regulation, from Ministerial Decision 115919 (2025) on agricultural workers and private shepherds; UAE confirmed from Federal Decree-Law 33/2021, art. 3. Six ILO farm conventions (C011, C099, C110, C129, C141, C184) re-checked on NORMLEX: no Gulf state is party."], ["1.3", "2026-11-11", "Kuwait, Bahrain and Oman checked against the ILO FAIRWAY factsheets on the regulatory framework for migrant workers (December 2023): Kuwait minimum wage recoded as in place (75 dinars, no nationality condition) and wage protection as partial (domestic workers outside); Bahrain wage protection recoded as partial. Farm work under domestic-worker law checked in official texts: Oman Ministerial Decision 574/2025, art. 2; Bahrain LMRA Order 4/2014, art. 2; UAE Federal Decree-Law 9/2022; Saudi Ministerial Decision 40676/1445. Bahrain fee ban (Law 19/2006, art. 23(C)) and Oman repeal of the 2004 domestic-worker rules noted. ILO C097, C143 and C189 non-ratification by all six states confirmed on NORMLEX (11 Nov 2026). Oman: Labour Law 53/2023 has no agricultural exclusion, so commercial farm workers are covered. Domestic laws database: 14 rows rechecked against official portals and three Saudi rows added (Ministerial Decisions 40676/1445, 212875/1443 and 115919 on agricultural workers and private shepherds); 72 instruments."], ["1.2", "2026-10-31", "Official-text check: Saudi and Qatari farmworker, mobility and wage-protection cells now rest on HRSD and Al Meezan texts; ILO ratifications (13 conventions) checked on NORMLEX; Palermo Protocol and Migrant Workers Convention status checked on the UN Treaty Collection. Economic context: remittances paid by each Gulf state (2015–2024) and, per corridor, the income gap, origin unemployment, youth unemployment, working-age share and remittance dependence (World Bank WDI, latest year 2019–2024). Bilateral remittance flows and corridor transfer costs are not yet included."], ["1.1", "2026-10-31", "Domestic laws database: 69 instruments with official or GLMM links; link status checked 31 Oct 2026."], ["1.0", "2026-10-31", "First release: six states coded on nine features; instruments, corridors and demography compiled."], ["1.0.1", "2026-10-31", "Reform tracker: four 2015–2016 entries (SA, QA, AE) added from Simmons & Simmons (2016)."]];
